# Post-reboot repair: revive colima, docker, Convex, k8s

flagg rebooted ~22:08 on 2026-07-30. You are on flagg. This is the critical
path: everything docker-hosted is down.

## Confirmed symptoms (steering, 06:11)

- `colima status` → fatal "colima is not running", yet launchd shows
  `com.joelclaw.colima` PID 364 exit 0. The launchd job likely ran and exited
  without colima actually up.
- `docker ps` → cannot connect to `~/.colima/default/docker.sock`.
- Self-hosted Convex at `http://127.0.0.1:3210` → connection refused. This is
  the gateway message-event stream; another worker is waiting on it.
- k8s (Talos on Colima) presumed down with docker.

## Levers (READ each script before running it)

- `infra/colima-start.sh` and `infra/launchd/com.joel.colima.plist`
- `infra/k8s-reboot-heal.sh` and `infra/launchd/com.joel.k8s-reboot-heal.plist`
- `infra/central/scripts/start-colima.sh`, `health.sh`, `diagnose.sh`,
  `recover.sh` (central stack tooling)
- Prefer restarting via the existing launchd label
  (`launchctl kickstart -k gui/501/<label>`) over ad-hoc `colima start`, so
  supervision stays where it was. If the plist itself is the bug, say so.

## Resolved when

1. `colima status` reports running and `docker ps` works.
2. Convex answers: `curl -sf http://127.0.0.1:3210/version` (or any 2xx/3xx).
3. k8s: `kubectl get nodes` shows Ready — ONLY if the cluster lives on this
   machine's colima. Fleet placement assigns `k8s` to panda; do NOT touch
   panda, do not declare panda's cluster broken (2026-07-14 false-fatal
   precedent). If flagg has no local cluster, record that and move on.
4. The daily-sidecar / wiki tailnet containers are up again (`docker ps`
   shows them; see `infra/daily-sidecar/` in joelclaw-wiki if needed).

## Rules

- No destructive commands. A dcg BLOCKED command is a full stop — report it.
- Do not commit anything.
- Do not delete or recreate VMs/volumes. If colima needs anything beyond a
  start/restart, STOP and report instead of improvising.
- Print a DONE summary: what was broken, what you ran, receipts (command +
  output snippets), what remains broken.

## Result (2026-07-31)

Delivered by pi worker (w28:p11). Colima restarted, docker back, Convex
backend healthy on :3210, daily-sidecar (wiki tailnet) containers up —
verified live by steering. Flagg has no local k8s (profile kubernetes:false);
panda untouched. Flagged: no user LaunchAgent supervises Joel's ~/.colima
profile (`com.joelclaw.colima` supervises /Users/joelclaw), so colima will
NOT survive the next power cycle; repo plist defaults differ from the live
profile (4c/8g/60g/ssh vs 8c/24g/100g/grpc). Convex LAN forwarder
(192.168.1.10:3210) absent; localhost + tailnet work.
